{"aligned_passages":[{"anchor":"weighted-tree","mapping_field":"claim_ids","mapping_ref":"sha256:3206447b7c5ce37e42a253ccbbdf9ea9fd64af6c402a7a116e30915fbcfcd2a4/papers/long.json","paper_href":"/api/v1/papers/long?manifest=4070c5207ff30ed1d5bf15d57c03035ee4c69363e55697fa8a2a1859ad2aa618","passage_ref":"sha256:fa472c25832b36a2061f212196277009f716c230a658520bb4b4f2ed8173d74b/papers/long.md/sha256:3206447b7c5ce37e42a253ccbbdf9ea9fd64af6c402a7a116e30915fbcfcd2a4/papers/long.json/passages/weighted-tree","query_href":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=4070c5207ff30ed1d5bf15d57c03035ee4c69363e55697fa8a2a1859ad2aa618&paper=long&passage=weighted-tree","reading_href":"/api/v1/papers/reading?manifest=4070c5207ff30ed1d5bf15d57c03035ee4c69363e55697fa8a2a1859ad2aa618&paper=long&passage=weighted-tree","span":{"end_byte":218569,"end_line":4813,"start_byte":208642,"start_line":4597},"stage":"long"}],"lenses":{"consumers":"/api/v1/graph?manifest=4070c5207ff30ed1d5bf15d57c03035ee4c69363e55697fa8a2a1859ad2aa618&view=arguments&node=circuit.weighted_finite_horizon&direction=consumers&assumptions=true","direct_passages":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=4070c5207ff30ed1d5bf15d57c03035ee4c69363e55697fa8a2a1859ad2aa618&node=circuit.weighted_finite_horizon&relation=direct","prerequisite_uses":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=4070c5207ff30ed1d5bf15d57c03035ee4c69363e55697fa8a2a1859ad2aa618&node=circuit.weighted_finite_horizon&relation=prerequisites","prerequisites":"/api/v1/graph?manifest=4070c5207ff30ed1d5bf15d57c03035ee4c69363e55697fa8a2a1859ad2aa618&view=arguments&node=circuit.weighted_finite_horizon&assumptions=true"},"neighborhood_href":"/api/v1/neighborhood?manifest=4070c5207ff30ed1d5bf15d57c03035ee4c69363e55697fa8a2a1859ad2aa618&ref=sha256%3A47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd%2Fnodes%2Fcircuit.weighted_finite_horizon","record":{"assumption_ids":[],"boundary":"Conditional ordinary reconstruction for the specified finite recursion, not a new formal theorem. The coefficient expectation uses the vertex law; its normalization uses the cavity law. Fixed-horizon and spatial-Lipschitz hypotheses are essential. The generic temporal-sign counterexample concerns auxiliary Theorem 4.1 as printed, not specialized positive-Parisi Proposition 4.7 or EAMS Theorem 1.7. No horizon-, temperature- or terminal-cutoff-uniform constant is claimed.","citation_ids":["circuit-r2-26-cite-positive-finite-step","eams2023_finite_step"],"evidence_ids":["ordinary_reconstruction_bounds_20261024"],"id":"circuit.weighted_finite_horizon","kind":"claim","label":"Corrected weighted finite-tree estimate with explicit hypotheses","locator":"07-positive-temperature.tex:211–450; EAMS arXiv:2111.06813v2 Proposition 2.1 and Lemmas 3.2–3.4,4.2–4.3; long §11.1","source_id":"circuit-r2-26-source-positive","statement":"In the specified EAMS one-step-lag recursion on a k-regular tree, k>=2, fix delta>0 and finite L>=1 with L*delta<1. Use iid Gaussian labels and the common node/cavity initial state sqrt(delta)*g_i. At the finitely many mesh times, assume |a_k|<=K>=1, spatial Lipschitz constants La,Lb for a_k,b_k uniform in k, identical normalized a_k for node/cavity updates, and E[(A_(i->j)^r)^2]=1. Then |k*E[z_o^L*z_v^L]-2*sqrt(k-1)*delta*sum_(r=1)^(L-1) E[B_o^r]|<=C(K,La,Lb,delta,L), independently of k. The sum is empty when L=1.","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/nodes/circuit.weighted_finite_horizon","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"citations","from":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/nodes/circuit.positive_finite_step","id":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/edges/%5B%22circuit.positive_finite_step%22%2C%22circuit.weighted_finite_horizon%22%2C%22cites%22%5D","kind":"cites","record_ref":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/edges/%5B%22circuit.positive_finite_step%22%2C%22circuit.weighted_finite_horizon%22%2C%22cites%22%5D","semantic_class":"citation_reference","to":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/nodes/circuit.weighted_finite_horizon"},{"derived":true,"family":"provenance","from":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/nodes/circuit.weighted_finite_horizon","id":"field:028f61fa7e7ebf758739584b79bc877b7e24a2ea3ca9bc1a1dd4a1d3f968e930","kind":"source_id","owner_ref":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/nodes/circuit.weighted_finite_horizon","semantic_class":"provenance_field_reference","source_field":"source_id","to":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/sources/circuit-r2-26-source-positive"},{"derived":true,"family":"provenance","from":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/nodes/circuit.weighted_finite_horizon","id":"field:2828a2fe84cde2033e0267fe6322e9893371e5ebf116fda7e2f59b6bf00ac784","kind":"evidence_ids","owner_ref":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/nodes/circuit.weighted_finite_horizon","semantic_class":"provenance_field_reference","source_field":"evidence_ids","to":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/evidence/ordinary_reconstruction_bounds_20261024"},{"derived":true,"family":"provenance","from":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/evidence/ordinary_reconstruction_bounds_20261024","id":"field:2fe2727b8f31f44ea94bdac7c0b518ab6f08ed66d3f60c43bdcb37cb4c7c4e33","kind":"subject_ids","owner_ref":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/evidence/ordinary_reconstruction_bounds_20261024","semantic_class":"provenance_field_reference","source_field":"subject_ids","to":"sha256:47eb5f9cd8936c095f37a279430757722203f6e0f60993eeefcb2953ffb994dd/nodes/circuit.weighted_finite_horizon"},{"derived":true,"family":"provenance","from":"sha256:47eb